From: meta-lubancat maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: make vendor driver paths survive out-of-tree builds

The Rockchip vendor wifi drivers only ever worked with S == B. Yocto builds
the kernel with O=${B}, which breaks them in two different ways, and both
failures look unrelated to their real cause:

1. Private header directories are added with `-I$(src)/...`, and `src` is a
   path relative to the source tree while the compiler runs with cwd =
   build tree. The flag therefore points at a directory that does not exist:

     rtl8821cu/core/rtw_cmd.c:17:10:
     fatal error: drv_types.h: No such file or directory

2. rtl8851be / rtl8852be derive DRV_PATH from `src` and then include their
   platform fragments with

     include $(wildcard $(DRV_PATH)/platform/*.mk)

   The wildcard is empty under O=, so platform/arm_rk.mk is never read and
   the driver loses -DCONFIG_IOCTL_CFG80211 / -DRTW_USE_CFG80211_STA_EVENT.
   Without them the code falls back to the pre-cfg80211-tracking path, which
   uses cfg80211_send_rx_assoc()/cfg80211_send_disassoc() (gone since 6.1)
   and still casts the adapter to a layout that no longer matches:

     rtw_swcrypto.c:16:10: fatal error: aes.h: No such file or directory
     ioctl_cfg80211.c:4948:32: error: 'struct _ADAPTER_LINK' has no member
     named 'mlmeext'

Note that relative `include $(src)/foo.mk` directives are fine: kbuild
exports MAKEFLAGS += --include-dir=$(abs_srctree). Only -I flags and
wildcards need the absolute path.

Resolve `src` to an absolute path once per makefile and use that for both.
The expression keeps working for `make M=...` module builds, where src is
already absolute.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BSP-specific]

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile
index ad8b07616905..7c2e11e8f915 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+# meta-lubancat: Yocto builds with O=${B}, so $(src) is relative to $(srctree)
+# and cannot be used directly in -I. Resolve it to an absolute path once.
+LUBANCAT_WIFI_SRC := $(if $(filter /%,$(src)),$(src),$(srctree)/$(src))
+
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += $(USER_EXTRA_CFLAGS)
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-implicit-fallthrough
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-variable
@@ -235,7 +239,7 @@ ccflags-$(CONFIG_VHT_FOR_OLD_KERNEL) += -DCONFIG_VHT_FOR_OLD_KERNEL
 ccflags-$(CONFIG_COEX) += -DCONFIG_COEX
 
 ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_RWNX_FULLMAC
-ccflags-y += -I$(src)/.
+ccflags-y += -I$(LUBANCAT_WIFI_SRC)/.
 ccflags-$(CONFIG_RWNX_RADAR) += -DCONFIG_RWNX_RADAR
 ccflags-$(CONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA) += -DCONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA
 ccflags-$(CONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT) += -DCONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT
